   - When we encounter an opening bracket (one of '(', '[', '{'), we push it onto the stack.
   - When we encounter a closing bracket (one of ')', ']', '}'), we check if it matches the most recent opening bracket by popping from the stack.

3. **Non-bracket Characters:**
   - Any character that isn't one of the six bracket characters is simply ignored (treated as valid).

4. **Complexity Analysis:**
   - **Time Complexity:** O(n) - We make a single pass through the string, performing constant-time operations for each character.
